From 726c2f953263bb806b42f9b9ae6b6bfb9489870b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:03:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] M10: the post effects: one full-screen shader for the glass
 and his eyes

GDD 16.4, with 16.3 and 5.8. A CanvasLayer "PostFX" in drive.tscn, over
the 3D view and under the pointer and the numeric HUD, runs
shaders/post_fx.gdshader through src/view/post_fx_view.gd (PostFxView).
It takes the nine uniforms from the snapshot once a frame:

- tunnel: dark edges close the view to tunnel_min_view at Nerves 100
- lids, blink: dark bars from the top and the bottom; they meet when his
  eyes are shut
- haze: a veil on the windscreen, smoke or dust, never thicker than the
  snapshot says
- rain_blur: the windscreen blurs between sweeps (the screen texture's
  mipmaps); rain falls outside every window
- cracks: a web fixed to the glass over that share of the windscreen
- glare_amount, glare_position: a wash and a blaze around the light
- darkness: the night outside the pool of the headlights

A canvas shader cannot read depth, so the glass is found by geometry:
the ray through each pixel is taken into the cabin frame and met with
three panes (tuning), less what is drawn under the Cabin's Mirror and
Visor nodes. The strip of windscreen just above the dash stays clear, so
the clock and what stands on the dash stay readable.

Every amount is eased, and one that has turned may not turn back for
postfx_flash_hold: no effect flashes faster than three times a second,
whatever the snapshot does. With nothing to show the rectangle is hidden
and the screen is not copied.

Every strength, colour and size is in data/tuning.json (post_fx_view).

tools/post_fx_shots.gd takes pictures of states set by hand over the
drive scene; tools/post_fx_check.gd checks the wiring and the flash rule
without a renderer. Pictures: artifacts/m10_postfx_*.png (darkness,
rain_blur and glare are legs driven by the simulation).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
